---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/company.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="FAQ" description="Answers about Chudware product scope, supported platforms, engineering files, AI provider configuration, subscriptions, and support.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Frequently asked</p>
      <h1>Answers before you install.</h1>
      <p class="lede">This page describes the product as it operates today. Detailed setup instructions live in the documentation.</p>
      <ul class="co-faq-jump">
        <li><a href="#co-product">The product</a></li>
        <li><a href="#co-access">Access and platforms</a></li>
        <li><a href="#co-files">Files and data</a></li>
        <li><a href="#co-ai">AI copilot</a></li>
        <li><a href="#co-commercial">Commercial and support</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-product">
    <div class="co-faq-group wrap">
      <h2 id="co-product" class="co-anchor">The product</h2>
      <details open>
        <summary>What is Chudware?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>An engineering workspace that combines parametric modeling, assemblies, drawings, CAM, simulation, PLM, reverse engineering, and an AI copilot. The native application and hosted browser workspace share the same product concepts and document format.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who is it for?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>Engineers and technical teams who need to create, inspect, manufacture, or manage product data. The product spans mechanical design, manufacturing, electronics, simulation, and adjacent engineering work rather than assuming one job title.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How mature is it?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>Chudware is in commercial preview. Core workflows are available, but file-format coverage and advanced study types continue to change. Use the trial on representative projects before moving production work.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What simulation studies are available?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>The engine provides static, adaptive and mesh-convergence FEA; modal and frequency-response studies; high-cycle fatigue; steady and transient thermal conduction; linear buckling; and contact-aware static studies. Built-in flow is useful for directional comparisons, while the OpenFOAM path provides the higher-fidelity external-aerodynamics route when OpenFOAM is installed. Read each study's mesh, convergence, reaction, and provenance output before using a result for a decision.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" aria-labelledby="co-access">
    <div class="co-faq-group wrap">
      <h2 id="co-access" class="co-anchor">Access and platforms</h2>
      <details open>
        <summary>What does the 14-day trial include?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>After email verification, a trial account can use the browser workspace and native desktop application for 14 days with 5 GB of account storage. No payment card is required.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which operating systems have published desktop builds?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>The stable release catalog currently publishes x86-64 builds for Windows, Linux, and macOS. The <a href="/download/">download page</a> reads the live release catalog and shows the exact version, package format, size, and checksum available for each platform.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What is the difference between Desktop and Studio?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>Desktop licenses the native application and includes 5 GB of account storage. Studio includes Desktop, adds the hosted browser workspace, and raises the storage quota to 100 GB. Both plans expose the same engineering workspaces.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do desktop downloads work?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>Sign in on the download page and choose the published build for your platform. Downloads use a short-lived, account-bound entitlement URL; the page also shows the SHA-256 checksum for independent verification.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-files">
    <div class="co-faq-group wrap">
      <h2 id="co-files" class="co-anchor">Files and data</h2>
      <details open>
        <summary>What is a <code>.step+</code> file?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>It is Chudware's portable project container. It carries neutral STEP geometry together with the feature recipe, parameters, metadata, thumbnails, and integrity information needed to continue editing in Chudware. The neutral STEP payload can be extracted or exported for exchange with another CAD system.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which exchange formats are supported?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>STEP is the primary neutral solid format. The product also exposes IGES, STL, OBJ, PLY, 3MF, GLB/glTF, BREP, and related formats where the selected workflow supports them. See the <a href="/product/modeling/#formats">format table</a> for the current import/export directions.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where are projects stored?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>Native desktop documents can stay on your workstation. Projects used in the hosted browser workspace are stored in your Chudware account and count against its storage quota. Export important work to your own project archive as part of normal backup practice.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I migrate existing work?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>Yes. Exchange a clean STEP model when you need exact solids, and use mesh formats only when a tessellated surface is sufficient. Imported neutral geometry does not recreate another CAD system's proprietary feature history, so retain the source file until the migrated project has been checked.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" aria-labelledby="co-ai">
    <div class="co-faq-group wrap">
      <h2 id="co-ai" class="co-anchor">AI copilot</h2>
      <details open>
        <summary>How does the copilot change a model?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>The copilot plans work, calls the same product tools available to the engineering workflow, and reads structured results. Geometry, simulation, and manufacturing operations still execute in the Chudware engine; generated text is not treated as proof that an operation succeeded.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do I connect an AI provider?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>Open Provider settings and connect a supported provider account or enter your own API key. Enter credentials only in that settings surface—never in chat, a prompt, or a project note. Available account and key connections are listed there.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who bills for AI usage?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>Your selected provider does. Its subscription, API prices, usage limits, and terms apply. Chudware does not currently sell AI token packs or managed model capacity.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What is sent to the provider?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>The prompt plus the project context and tool results needed for the current turn are sent to the provider you selected. Chudware does not send your provider credential as prompt text. Review the provider's privacy and retention terms before using confidential project data.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Should I accept copilot output without review?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>No. Inspect the feature tree, dimensions, toolpaths, boundary conditions, mesh quality, reactions, and exported evidence appropriate to the task. The copilot can execute and inspect work; the engineer remains responsible for the design and release decision.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="co-commercial">
    <div class="co-faq-group wrap">
      <h2 id="co-commercial" class="co-anchor">Commercial and support</h2>
      <details open>
        <summary>How do I see the current subscription price?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>Desktop and Studio are monthly self-service subscriptions. Authenticated checkout shows the current rate before purchase, including the education rate for an eligible verified <code>.edu</code> account. Enterprise accounts are arranged directly. See <a href="/pricing/">pricing</a> for plan scope.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do cancellation and refunds work?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>You can cancel a subscription from the billing portal; access continues through the period already paid for. Refund requests are handled under the published <a href="/legal/refunds/">refund policy</a>.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where can I get help?</summary>
        <div class="co-answer"><p>Start with the <a href="/docs/">documentation</a> and <a href="/docs/troubleshooting/">troubleshooting guide</a>. For account or product help, email <a href="mailto:support@chudware.com">support@chudware.com</a>. Security reports go to <a href="mailto:security@chudware.com">security@chudware.com</a>.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="wrap section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Still deciding?</p>
      <h2>Use a representative project during the trial.</h2>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://app.chudware.com/signup">Start the trial</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/contact/">Contact Chudware</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
